{"name":"Early July","hex":"#a5ddea","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"early","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["At a time in advance of the usual or expected event.","Arriving a time before expected; sooner than on time."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shift (scheduled work period) that takes place early in the day."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/early"}],"entries":[{"title":"July","blocks":[{"text":"July is the seventh month of the year in the Julian and Gregorian calendars. Its length is 31 days. It was named by the Roman Senate in honour of Roman general and statesman Julius Caesar in 44 B.C., being the month of his birth. Before then it was called Quintilis, being the fifth month of the calendar that started with March."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/July","wikidata":"Q121"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Ruby_gem.JPG/330px-Ruby_gem.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Ruby_gem.JPG/330px-Ruby_gem.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ruby gemstone","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARuby_gem.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Baker%27s_Larkspur_%285933879987%29.jpg/500px-Baker%27s_Larkspur_%285933879987%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Baker%27s_Larkspur_%285933879987%29.jpg/1280px-Baker%27s_Larkspur_%285933879987%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Baker%27s_Larkspur_%285933879987%29.jpg/500px-Baker%27s_Larkspur_%285933879987%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Blue delphinium (Larkspur)",